  "hypothesis": "A gap’s immediate slack is an incomplete proxy for reusable capacity. Empirical per-size demand adjusted for the number of currently fitting gaps, plus a global observed deletion hazard, may rank existing large-state choices better by expected future reusable space, especially in mixed-size/high-fragmentation states. It uses only past operations and current free gaps; it has no test identity or future-trace dispatch.",
  "causality": "At query time, use only the prior 2048 valid events and current coalesced gap counts. Demand rate lambda_s divides recent requests of size s by the count of gaps that fit s; expiry uses recent deletes per live pipe. The DP marginal value ranks only current distinct-size representatives after the strong seed’s existing structural gates. Current request is added to the model only after placement.",
